\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb240\sa120{\loch
1. What TLO Inventory does}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
TLO Inventory provides full inventory, incremental Add Shows processing, audio tagging, inventory searching, log research, confirmed logged folder reversal, and auxiliary Artist, City and Venue database searching. The source bundle contains the TLO application sources, tests, documentation, and application distribution utilities. The independently versioned GitHub Build Process is distributed separately and is not included in the TLO source bundle. The separate distribution ZIP contains native end-user applications for Windows, macOS, and generic Linux. The generic Linux applications are also used when running under WSL; there is no separate WSL application directory or WSL build.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
The full inventory function scans configured music roots, identifies core show metadata, prepares searchable setlist text, and builds the inventory output used by the included search tools.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
Full Inventory scans configured music roots and rebuilds the inventory outputs.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
Add Shows adds new content to an existing inventory without rerunning the full scan. When a show is moved between different disks or filesystems, TLO first stages and verifies the entire copy using sizes and SHA-256 hashes. It deletes the original only after the verified folder has been published. If source cleanup fails after publication, both paths may exist; reconcile them manually before retrying. Transfers involving symbolic links are refused for safety.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
GUI Tag and inventory-time tagging write audio metadata when you choose to tag files. GUI Tag uses the selected main Tag In Place, Tag Copy, or Tag Copy/Delete Original mode. Standalone tlo-tag remains a direct-path command-line tagger and does not use the GUI copy modes.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
The included Search app searches the completed bootlist and setlist files after the distribution is extracted into TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl276\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
Research searches the comp and meta logs by artist plus date, venue, or date and is available from the Main GUI and the standalone tlo-research console app.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb240\sa120{\loch
2. Quick Start}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
Use this path for a first inventory configured to avoid file/folder mutation. The detailed installation, volume-name, and option sections follow later in the manual.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
1. Windows: install the signed TLO MSI (recommended). Linux/WSL and macOS: extract the matching complete portable ZIP into TLOHome. Windows users who prefer a portable installation may also extract the matching ZIP. Never run TLO directly from inside an archive.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
2. Confirm that TLOHome/TLO_DBs contains artists.sqlite, venues.txt, cities.sqlite, and venues.sqlite. City-only recognition uses the date already identified by the inventory parser, including its original date spelling; it does not guess new dates or override existing venue/location fields. Windows MSI installations may place the applications outside TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
3. Configure TLOHome, using the installer folder picker on Windows MSI, a TLOHome environment variable, or --TLOHome followed by the full folder path. For portable Windows, one example is "C:\\.tlo\\apps\\Windows\\tlo-main.exe" --TLOHome "C:\\.tlo". For Linux/WSL, use "$HOME/TLOHome/apps/Linux/tlo-main" --TLOHome "$HOME/TLOHome". See https://traderslittleorganizer.com for additional help.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
4. In Path(s), enter one or more semicolon-separated roots, or a fully qualified .txt control file. For external drives, a matching visible volume label such as [Archive]E:\\Music is recommended. Native Windows UNC shares (\\\\server\\share\\folder) are also supported without a mapped drive letter.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
5. Start the Main GUI. Artist In Album Tag is the only checkbox selected by default. If you do not want to move any corrupt files or folders to the Trash/Recycle Bin during a normal Inventory run, set Corrupt files to Keep and report. This also makes Folder removal effectively Never. The default corruption settings are Keep and report for files, Never for folders. On native Windows, if TLO cannot confirm that the selected drive has a usable Recycle Bin and adequate quota, it retains the show and reports that recycling is unavailable. Removable, network, unsupported, and unconfirmed volumes are retained; TLO does not fall back to permanent deletion.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
6. Select Dry Run and click Inventory. Review the proposed show names, any planned tags, and corruption actions. Dry Run never moves, Trashes, or deletes files or folders, regardless of the Corruption Handling settings.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
7. Clear Dry Run and click Inventory again when the review is satisfactory. Confirm the settings in Review Operation and click Start.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
8. After completion, open TLOHome/bootlist.csv, TLOHome/setlists, the completion summary, and View Issues. Detailed logs are under TLOHome/logs.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\qc\sb0\sa60{\loch
Main window reference: Path(s) accepts multiple semicolon-separated paths and the documented /slam syntax. Use the current on-screen controls; obsolete screenshots have been omitted.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
Recycle Bin safety: On Windows, TLO verifies local NTFS, Explorer recycling settings and available Recycle Bin quota before sending corrupt material to the Recycle Bin. A failed check or failed recycle stops further corruption-driven removal for that show, keeps affected files in place, and suppresses other mutations. Under WSL, gio normally uses the Linux/WSL Trash location rather than the Windows Recycle Bin; Trash on a mounted Windows volume may use a .Trash directory on that volume or fail. Check the local environment and logs rather than assuming Windows Recycle Bin recovery.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
First-run safety: Dry Run performs metadata and tag planning but does not write or probe tags, convert SHN files, rename folders, copy, move, Trash, or delete content, or replace inventory output. If sibling release/disc folders would be consolidated, Dry Run describes the proposed parent, how many child folders would be combined, and flags existing group predictions as provisional. TLO Reverse does not currently undo sibling collection consolidations. This guarantee does not depend on the Corruption Handling policy. Dry Run never probes tags or decodes audio, even when Deep Audio Check is selected.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb240\sa120{\loch
3. Installation package and TLOHome layout}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
Distribution options: Windows normally uses a signed MSI installer. Portable complete/update ZIP archives remain available for Windows, generic Linux/WSL, and macOS. ZIP names identify the build, package kind and platform; use a complete ZIP for a new portable installation and the correct update ZIP for an existing portable installation. Windows updater downloads MSI by default, including from a ZIP installation.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
The source bundle contains the requirements DOCX, the current RTF user manual, TLO source, tests, and distribution utilities. The independently versioned GitHub Build Process is packaged separately; no build-process artifact is included in this source bundle.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
TLOHome/\line   TLO_DBs/\line     artists.sqlite\line     venues.txt\line     cities.sqlite\line     venues.sqlite\line   bootlist.csv\line   setlists/  logs/  dups/  readyForXfer/\line   tlo-preferences.ini\line \line Portable ZIP installations also include:\line   apps/Windows/   (Windows executables and runtimes)\line   apps/Linux/     (Linux and WSL executables)\line   apps/macOS/     (macOS executables and .app bundles)\line \line Windows MSI installs its applications in the user's local Programs area, not within TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
Complete portable distributions include the Search, Research, Reverse, Tag, Inventory, and duplicate-cleanup utilities, plus artists.sqlite, venues.txt, cities.sqlite and venues.sqlite. WSL uses the generic Linux build. The Windows hybrid package uses seven PyInstaller onefile executables plus tlo-deleteDupes.cmd and its adjacent tlo-deleteDupes_runtime private Python runtime. The Windows onedir package uses seven executables and a shared _internal runtime folder, plus the same duplicate-cleanup launcher/runtime files. Keep the runtime files with their launchers, and replace apps/Windows as a complete unit when changing layouts. macOS includes tlo-main.app, tlo-search.app, and searchAuxDBs.app alongside command-line tools.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8316\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Do not run inside the ZIP: Always extract the installation ZIP first. Windows and Linux cannot reliably execute the apps while dependencies, databases, or shell scripts are still compressed.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa60\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa60\loch

\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
TLOHome also contains update-settings.json, unidentifiedShows.txt, artistsNotInDatabase.txt, deletedDirs.txt, and other generated inventory and diagnostic files. The TLO_DBs directory is installer-managed on Windows MSI installations; back up user-modified databases before an upgrade.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb240\sa120{\loch
4. Pre-installation checklist}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
Choose the final TLOHome folder. Use a short absolute path such as C:\\TLOHome on Windows or $HOME/TLOHome on WSL/Linux.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
Confirm that TLOHome is writable by the account that will run the apps.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
Know how attached drives will be mounted. Windows runs can use drive-letter paths such as E:\\Music. WSL/Linux runs can use paths such as /mnt/e/Music after the drive is mounted and visible to that environment.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
Use visible and unique volume names for search roots. They are strongly recommended, especially with external drives, backup drives, WSL paths, or drives that may get different letters over time.}
\par \pard\plain \s58\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1\fi-259\li360\lin360\sb0\sa40\contextualspace{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
If setlist.fm lookup will be used, obtain a setlist.fm API key and set SETLISTFM_API_KEY before starting the GUI. To enable setlist.fm Upgrade, also set SETLISTFMUPGRADE_API_KEY (or SETLISTFM_UPGRADE_API_KEY) to the same API key value. If the normal key is missing, both setlist.fm controls are unchecked and greyed out. If the accepted upgrade variable is missing or does not match SETLISTFM_API_KEY, normal setlist.fm remains available and only setlist.fm Upgrade is greyed out. The GUI explains whether the normal key is missing, the upgrade key is missing, or the two values do not match, without displaying either key. On Windows an explicit nonblank CMD/PowerShell/process value takes precedence; current persisted User/System values are used only as fallback when the corresponding process value is missing or blank because the launching parent has a stale environment snapshot.}
\par \trowd\trqc\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\clcbpat23\cellx8316\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa20{\loch
Installation contents: The installation ZIP installs the application files and support folders under TLOHome. Pre-installation setup is limited to choosing a writable TLOHome location, preparing environment variables, and making sure mounted drives will be visible.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl252\slmult1\sb0\sa60\loch

\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb240\sa120{\loch
5. Windows installation and shortcuts}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb180\sa80{\loch
Windows MSI installation (recommended)}
\par \pard\plain \s61\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
1. Download the signed TLO MSI from the official GitHub release and run it. Follow the installation dialog, including the TLOHome choice when prompted.}
\par \pard\plain \s61\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
2. TLO applications are installed outside TLOHome. Existing inventory data, preferences, and setlists in TLOHome are preserved during MSI upgrades and uninstall. The MSI installs all four database files directly in TLOHome/TLO_DBs before any application launches, replaces those files on upgrade, and removes its managed files on uninstall. Back up database customizations before upgrading. Applications read only the active TLOHome/TLO_DBs and never copy database masters. A command-line override must already contain the appropriate database files.}
\par \pard\plain \s61\loch\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa200\contextualspace\sl240\slmult1{\hich\af3\loch\f3\loch
3. Launch TLO Main from its Start-menu shortcut. If upgrading from a portable ZIP installation, the old TLOHome/apps directory is not removed automatically and may be deleted manually after confirming the MSI installation works.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb180\sa80{\loch
Windows portable ZIP installation (optional)}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
1.\tab Create or choose the TLOHome folder, for example C:\\TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
2.\tab Extract the installation ZIP so the apps and support folders appear inside TLOHome.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
3.\tab Confirm that C:\\TLOHome\\apps\\Windows contains tlo-main.exe, tlo-gi.exe, tlo-research.exe, tlo-reverse.exe, tlo-tag.exe, tlo-deleteDupes.cmd, tlo-search.exe, and searchAuxDBs.exe.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
4.\tab Set the TLOHome environment variable and optional variables described in Section 7.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
5.\tab Open a new Windows terminal or restart any already-open TLO app so the changed environment is visible.}
\par \pard\plain \s72\rtlch\af12\afs17\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af8\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb40\sa80\ltrpar\cf0\f8\fs17\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af13\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi0\li360\lin360\ri144\rin144\sb60\sa120{\loch
PowerShell example:\line Expand-Archive .\\TLO_V1.7Build<BUILD>_complete_Windows.zip -DestinationPath C:\\TLOHome\line setx TLOHome "C:\\TLOHome"\line setx TLOCurrentStorage "Backup-1"\line setx SETLISTFM_API_KEY "your-api-key-if-used"\line setx SETLISTFMUPGRADE_API_KEY "same-api-key-if-upgrade-is-used"}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb180\sa80{\loch
Optional Windows shortcuts}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
After installation, you may pin tlo-main.exe or tlo-search.exe from TLOHome\\apps\\Windows to Start. Set the shortcut Start in field to TLOHome\\apps\\Windows. Windows, not TLO, controls shortcut hot keys and Startup-folder behavior.}
\par \pard\plain \s1\rtlch\af12\afs32\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb480\sa0\keepn\cf17\f4\fs32\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb240\sa120{\loch
6. macOS, Linux, and WSL installation}
\par \pard\plain \s2\rtlch\af12\afs26\ab \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\sl240\slmult1\keep\sb200\sa0\keepn\cf18\f4\fs26\b\dbch\af9\sl240\slmult1\sb180\sa80{\loch
Install or refresh TLOHome}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
1.\tab Create or choose the TLOHome folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
2.\tab Extract the matching complete package, such as TLO_V1.7Build<BUILD>_complete_Linux.zip or TLO_V1.7Build<BUILD>_complete_macOS.zip, directly into that folder.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\fi-360\li360\lin360\sb0\sa60{\loch
