Required inventory input. Enter one direct root or multiple entries separated by semicolons. Direct entries may start with [Volume] and may include the same --/slam, --/copy, or --/copy-delete directives used in control files. An entry ending in .txt is read as an inventory-control file using the former toBeInventoried format; any .txt filename is accepted. TLOHome/toBeInventoried.txt is not read automatically.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft97\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5267\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10436\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Inline --/slam}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
There is no separate GUI Slam field. Put --/slam ARTIST_NAME on the applicable Path(s) entry, using the same syntax as toBeInventoried.txt. For a .txt control file, put --/slam on the applicable line inside the file.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft97\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5267\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10436\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Performance Mode}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
gentle, balanced, fast, or extreme. GUI default is balanced.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft97\ltrrow\trkeep\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5267\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadft3\clpadt108\clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrcf1\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10436\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Max Workers}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Maximum worker ceiling. At GUI startup, a positive launcher value is shown if supplied; otherwise the field starts at the selected Performance Mode's automatic ceiling. Selecting a Performance Mode resets the field to that mode's automatic ceiling. Runtime rules may use fewer workers; the ceiling does not force that many workers.}\cell\row\pard \trowd\trql\trleft97\ltrrow\trpaddft3\trpaddt0\trpaddfl3\trpaddl0\trpaddfb3\trpaddb0\trpaddfr3\trpaddr0\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx5267\clpadft3\clpadt108\clpadfr3\clpadr108\cellx10436\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Corruption Handling}\cell\pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\intbl\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa200{\loch
Grouped controls for proven corruption: Corrupt files chooses Keep and report or Delete corrupt files; Folder removal chooses Never, 100% corrupt only, or At threshold; Folder corruption threshold is 0-100. When Keep and report is selected, Folder removal is effectively Never and both folder-removal controls are greyed out. With Delete corrupt files selected, Folder removal is available and the threshold value is enabled only for At threshold. The Corrupt files drop-down is only slightly wider than the compact control and is sized to avoid clipping the end of Delete corrupt files; the Folder removal drop-down remains compact, the threshold label is single-line, and the % sign sits immediately beside the threshold value box. Defaults are Keep and report for files and Never for folders.}\cell\row\pard \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl276\slmult1\sb0\sa60{\loch
On Linux, a folder name containing filesystem bytes that are not valid UTF-8 cannot be recorded in the UTF-8 inventory. TLO reports it as UNIDENTIFIED_NON_UTF8_PATH (with the raw filesystem-path bytes in hexadecimal) in unidentifiedShows.txt and the dead-end log instead of silently ignoring it. Rename that folder to a valid UTF-8 name before re-inventorying. Dry Run reports the warning without writing unidentifiedShows.txt. Corruption Handling separates folder decisions from individual-file decisions. When tagging or Deep Audio Check is enabled, TLO classifies the original audio population as healthy, proven corrupt, or unverifiable; otherwise there is no corruption checking. Folder removal is evaluated first from that untouched snapshot: Never removes no folder because of corruption; 100% corrupt only removes a logical show or direct music folder only when its evaluated audio population is entirely corrupt; At threshold removes it when the proven-corruption percentage is greater than or equal to Folder corruption threshold. Only content that remains then reaches Corrupt files: Keep and report leaves proven-corrupt files in place and logs them, while Delete corrupt files moves the remaining corrupt files to the OS Trash/Recycle Bin. A failed folder Trash does not override Keep and report. Missing, locked, unreadable, disconnected, resource-failed, or validator-infrastructure-failed files are unverifiable, suppress corruption-driven Trash, and fail closed before later mutation. MP3 and FLAC share the same corruption population and Keep/Delete and Never/100%/threshold policies. Normal non-tagging validation checks headers/metadata only; a passing header does not establish full audio-stream integrity. Actual tagging additionally tests reversible tag writability; Deep Audio Check optionally verifies the full audio stream. When a real tagging mode is active, TLO also verifies tag writability before mutation by saving a temporary private test tag, reopening it, restoring the exact prior value or absence, and reopening again to verify restoration. Deep Audio Check is a separate default-off checkbox directly beneath Proper Grammar. When selected, TLO fully decodes the audio using the bundled ffmpeg. For FLAC recordings with a declared, nonzero STREAMINFO sample total, TLO also compares the count of actual decoded audio samples with that declaration: a shorter decoded stream is corrupt even when ffmpeg exits successfully. A declared sample count of zero means the length was not supplied, not that the audio is corrupt. An unreadable required sample-count report, an unavailable decoder, timeout, cancellation, access/I/O failure, or decoder infrastructure failure is unverifiable and fails closed rather than authorizing deletion. Other codecs receive full decoding, although a successful decoder exit cannot prove completeness when no authoritative expected duration or sample count exists. When Deep Audio Check is off, non-tagging inventory remains header/metadata validation only. Header/metadata failures are corruption; an unreadable or inaccessible file due to permissions, I/O, or unavailable validation components is unverifiable and fails closed. Dry Run never writes the temporary test tag and never moves/deletes anything, regardless of Corruption Handling settings. A FLAC with an unset STREAMINFO MD5 is not inherently corrupt or untaggable. If its temporary tag is saved, reopened, restored and verified, and the entire audio stream decodes successfully with no sample-count mismatch, TLO permits ordinary tagging. It logs DEEP_AUDIO_CHECK_MD5_UNSET because there is no stored checksum with which to authenticate the decoded audio. This is a decode-only check, not proof of perfect audio, and cannot by itself cause deletion. A genuine non-access tag-write failure is still treated as corruption. Filesystem failures, incomplete checks and timeouts remain unverifiable and block mutation.}
