The main window displays the checkboxes in five logical rows, as one compact block to the right of Performance Mode and Max Workers. Each checkbox indicator aligns with the top text line of its label. The first-column sequence etreeDB, setlist.fm, setlist.fm Upgrade, and Thorough Setlist Matching uses the same compact vertical row spacing all the way down; the wrapped Tag Copy/Delete Original label does not make the third row taller and push Thorough farther down. Thorough Setlist Matching and Tag Copy/Delete Original use two-line labels, and the new Delete Extra Tags checkbox uses a two-line label in row 4, column 4 at the far right. Checkbox widget and row padding remain minimized without overlap; established checkbox placements remain unchanged and Deep Audio Check occupies the new fifth-row cell beneath Proper Grammar. The boxed Corruption Handling group now runs as one single horizontal strip directly beneath the performance/checkbox options: Corrupt files followed immediately by its drop-down, Folder removal followed immediately by its drop-down, then Folder corruption threshold followed immediately by the compact value box and % sign. The threshold control is disabled unless Folder removal is At threshold. No default corruption summary is shown below the group; validation errors still appear. At startup, TLO constructs the main window while hidden, then maps and normalizes it before applying the initial screen fit. TLO lifts the mapped window and repeats the map/fit/lift stabilization once after Tk and the desktop window manager become idle. This keeps the first visible window within the current screen and avoids Linux/X11/Wayland cases where a Tk application can appear only in a task switcher or thumbnail. The only Thorough-specific main-window Info line appears when Thorough Setlist Matching and setlist.fm are checked while setlist.fm Upgrade is not checked; it warns that Thorough matching will be slow under the normal 600-ms / 1,400-call limits unless setlist.fm Upgrade is enabled. No Thorough-specific Info line appears for etreeDB-only use, when setlist.fm is off, when setlist.fm Upgrade is on, or when Thorough is off. Row 1, left to right: etreeDB, Compliant, Tag In Place, Artist In Album Tag. Row 2: setlist.fm, Rename Compliantly, Tag Copy, Convert shn. Row 3: setlist.fm Upgrade, As-Is Artist Name, Tag Copy/Delete Original, Dry Run. Row 4: Thorough Setlist Matching in column 1, Proper Grammar in column 2 directly beneath As-Is Artist Name, column 3 occupied by the wrapped Tag Copy/Delete Original control, and Delete Extra Tags in column 4. Row 5 contains Deep Audio Check in column 2 directly beneath Proper Grammar. Deep Audio Check, Thorough Setlist Matching, and Delete Extra Tags default off; Artist In Album Tag remains the only checkbox selected by default. The setlist.fm Upgrade checkbox is directly beneath setlist.fm and has effect only while setlist.fm is enabled. Compliant and Rename Compliantly are mutually exclusive: checking either one automatically unchecks the other. Delete Extra Tags is greyed out and unchecked whenever Tag In Place, Tag Copy, and Tag Copy/Delete Original are all unchecked. Selecting any one of those three tagging modes enables Delete Extra Tags. The three tagging modes remain mutually exclusive.}
