TLOHome/CorruptFlacs.txt is an append-only diagnostic file stored in the TLOHome root (not in TLOHome/logs); it records full paths of FLAC or MP3 files that could not be opened or written. Log tokens are assigned per active search path. Labeled-volume reruns replace or prune the affected scope according to path relationships, but first preserve folder rename/copy history in TLOHome/logs/folderOperations.log for tlo-reverse. If archiving fails, TLO leaves the prior operation log unchanged. Log tokens retain the legacy 0-9 and A-Z single-character names. After those 36 are used, TLO allocates multi-character tokens beginning with 10 and supporting up to 1,296 token values; old log names are preserved. Keep old logs for Reverse history rather than deleting them. Blank-label runs append to the shared blank-volume log set and can create duplicates if the same content is scanned again.}
