\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\sb0\sa60\loch

\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\af14\afs24 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\cf1\b\f4\dbch\af14\loch
International dates and disc folders}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa0{\rtlch\af14\afs24 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\cf1\b0\f4\dbch\af14\loch
TLO accepts German, French, and Italian month names as well as English: 01. Juni 2022, 1er juin 2022, and 1 maggio 2022 are valid dates. In conservative date parsing, month-only Mars or Juli is too ambiguous to establish a performance date; a clear day-first or year-first complete date is preferred. Adjacent complete dates joined by a spaced dash are not merged into an invented hybrid date. Compliant mode groups Disc 01/Disc 02, CD1/CD2, or Set 1/Set 2 below the same identified show, without requiring a setlist. Unrelated or incomplete groups remain separate.}{\rtlch\af14\afs24 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\cf1\b\f4\dbch\af14\loch
Date and startup safety}
\par \pard\plain \s0\rtlch\af12\afs20\alang1033 \ltrch\lang1033\langfe1033\hich\af2\loch\sl276\slmult1\ql\widctlpar\hyphpar0\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\cf0\f2\fs20\lang1033\kerning0\dbch\af10\langfe1033\sl240\slmult1\ql\sb0\sa160{\rtlch\af14\afs24 \ltrch\hich\af4\loch\cf1\b0\f4\dbch\af14\loch
The word Gen in a tape source-lineage description is not a month or performance date. Full German, French and Italian month names remain recognized. Windows and WSL representations of TLOHome are protected from generated folder-deletion scripts. If Windows TkDND is unavailable, the Main GUI opens normally but file drag-and-drop is disabled; keyboard and paste entry continue working.}
\par \par \b Safe Renaming, Search View, and Worker Recovery\b0\par
Rename Compliantly is conservative. A folder is not renamed when the identified show is uncertain or the proposed name would lose a known year or date, city/venue, or source qualifier (SBD, AUD, matrix, FM). A skipped rename leaves original files untouched. A stable compliant folder is not renamed repeatedly merely due to punctuation changes; capitalization-only correction is still allowed.\par
Search View uses setlist-index.json with the exact Show and VolumePath to open the correct setlist when two performances have the same displayed Show. Keep setlist-index.json with bootlist.csv and the setlists folder when copying TLOHome. If old data has multiple identical Show rows but no index, Search will not guess which setlist belongs to a selected row; re-inventory the affected source to regenerate the mapping. bootlist.csv remains a two-column caret-separated CSV.\par
Search permits ordinary apostrophes such as Gilley's and parenthetical qualifiers such as (Early Show) in literal searches. Explicit |AND| and |OR| expressions are still supported. Excessively complex expressions produce a specific search error instead of a recursion failure.\par
If a parallel worker stops unexpectedly, completed mutations may remain on disk but the bootlist and setlists are not finalized. Non-mutating unfinished paths can be retried serially. TLO stops without replaying uncertain mutating work. Inspect affected paths and re-inventory deliberately.\par

\par\b Installed shortcuts and inventory integrity\b0\par
On Windows MSI installation, the Traders Little Organizer Start Menu group includes TLO Auxiliary Database Search, which starts searchAuxDBs.exe.\par
Rename Compliantly preserves known dates, numeric recording identifiers and source-resolution qualifiers, and skips uncertain renames. A positively identified short artist/date trading folder such as trey05-12-02.flac can become the full show name; a plain media-format suffix is not an identifying qualifier, and a verified unique Artist DB alias can expand to its selected artist. Two distinct agreeing full-date track filenames can settle a single ambiguous short folder date when no selected setlist supplies a date. Track filenames remain unchanged.\par
Child-path re-inventory preserves Reverse history for other paths; multiple-path prompts default to Skip.\par
Invalid bootlist.csv encoding is detected before changes: re-save as CSV UTF-8. The bootlist file is replaced atomically, and names beginning with spreadsheet formula characters are escaped in the file but displayed normally in Search.\par

\par\b Identity, Search, and worker recovery\b0\par
Rename Compliantly keeps show names stable when the proposed name would only discard venue punctuation. When the folder does not change, the Album tag and bootlist Show follow the retained spelling. Other uncertain renames remain skipped.\par
International names with accents are compared consistently, and non-Latin artist or location words are preserved. Month words may be normalized only when a real date is recognized; source identity words such as Brian May and New Riders remain protected.\par
Search accepts curly and straight apostrophes, extra spacing and nested parenthesized qualifiers in Boolean expressions. For an older inventory with multiple identical Show names but no setlist index, View displays instructions to re-inventory the affected volume; it does not guess a setlist.\par
Rename Compliantly prints renamed/skipped counts and writes the same summary to the tag log and summary.log; detailed skip reasons appear in the tag error log. After a mutating worker crash, already changed folders and tags may be present, but bootlist.csv and setlists are not finalized; inspect and re-inventory deliberately.\par
\par\b Search messages and city catalog\b0\par Search error handling: malformed Boolean expressions are identified as Search errors, not problems with the inventory file. If bootlist.csv is not UTF-8, Search identifies the file and advises re-saving it as CSV UTF-8 before retrying. Search shows actual names starting with +, -, =, or @ rather than the protective apostrophe stored in the CSV file. Search does not alter the CSV when a read error occurs. City lookup uses the physical cities.sqlite catalog; it is not embedded in the executable.\par
\par\b Multi-day date validation\b0\par Multi-day performance dates: A folder date range such as November 17-18, 2026 is accepted when both calendar dates are valid and are not in the future. A range that includes a future date, even if the first day is today, is not treated as a known performance date. TLO leaves unresolved dates unresolved instead of guessing; no folder rename should be justified by an invalid future range.\par
\par \pard\plain \f2\fs22\b Interrupted Windows transfers\b0\par When a Tag Copy/Delete move was interrupted, use tlo-reverse --recover-staging --dry-run to inspect recovery; only then invoke without --dry-run. Windows now checks whether the recorded worker still exists without sending a Ctrl+C event. Conflicting or uncertain owner status is never restored automatically.\par \par \pard\plain \f2\fs22\b Deep Audio Check: unset MD5\b0\par An unset FLAC checksum does NOT mean the file is untaggable or corrupt. If BOTH the stored audio MD5 and sample count are unset (common with piped encoding), Deep Audio Check cannot prove all audio was decoded, even if a tag probe succeeds. TLO reports the file as unverifiable and suppresses deletion and further tagging in that run. Normal tagging without Deep Audio Check still uses its reversible tag-write test. A non-access tag-write failure is treated as corruption.\par \par \pard\plain \f2\fs22\b Search spelling and city labels\b0\par Search accepts accented names copied from setlist pages (such as Bjork with an umlaut) and finds the corresponding ASCII show names. When a recognized city is followed by an SBD, AUD, disc, set or sample-rate qualifier, TLO retains the city in the Show and ALBUM rather than dropping it. Original source labels remain protected against lossy renaming.\par \par \pard\plain \f2\fs22\b Run summaries, Search and Recovery preview\b0\par The Rename Compliantly count in summary.log reflects the volumes handled by the current run, not earlier inventories of other volumes. Boolean Search reports an unmatched closing parenthesis as an error; normal pasted show names retain their literal parentheses. Staged move recovery with --recover-staging --dry-run reports how many folders would be restored without moving any data.\par \par \pard\plain \f2\fs22\b Stable ALBUM and Show after another inventory\b0\par A venue containing internal punctuation such as Barton Hall, Cornell University retains that punctuation after a second or subsequent inventory. The folder, bootlist Show and audio ALBUM remain consistent whether the follow-up is Rename Compliantly with tagging, tagging alone, or a plain inventory. If identification remains uncertain or a proposed rename would discard source information, TLO still leaves the folder unchanged.\par \par \pard\plain \f2\fs22\b Cross-platform inventory testing\b0\par A search path without a bracketed volume label uses the label reported by the operating system. If you explicitly provide a bracketed label, it must match the actual mounted volume when that identity is available. A mismatch is refused to avoid inventorying the wrong disk. This rule is unchanged; A prior build corrected the automated repeated-inventory test to use the reported volume label when one exists and a stable test label when the operating system reports none.\par \par\b Current security and installation notes\b0\par Windows MSI configures TLOHome; the executables are installed separately. For portable builds, configure TLOHome before launch. All complete installations require artists.sqlite, venues.txt, cities.sqlite, and venues.sqlite under TLOHome/TLO_DBs. Source-only ZIPs carry database placeholders and are not runnable distributions.\par Copy Requests refuses paths outside a mapped volume root, including parent traversal and symlinked ancestor escapes. Staging recovery requires an independent issuance record; older interrupted moves without this record need manual review. Non-Latin artist folder/tag changes are conservatively skipped to protect existing tags. Deep Audio Check may leave unverifiable audio unchanged and report the reason.\par\par\b Portability and recovery refinements\b0\par Manual Tweaks rejects folder names invalid on Windows even when run on another platform. Search removes Latin accents but retains non-Latin vowel and accent marks. Copy Request destination locks clear owner details on successful release. Recovery records process creation identity when available to guard against Windows PID reuse. The source candidate is not a signed installer.\par\par\par\b City-only location parsing and Dry Run\b0\par When artist/date and a complete city-catalog match are known, TLO can ignore recognized trailing recording annotations such as [FLAC16], SBD, or 24-96. Ambiguous venue/city divisions remain unidentified. Dry Run flags only genuine multi-member sibling consolidations. Add Shows failures during verified staging retain the original folder.\par\par\b Rename Compliantly and fallback titles\b0\par Exact equivalent dates such as 98-05-08, 8. Mai 1998 and 1er avril 1998 may be normalized to YYYY-MM-DD. Different dates, shnid values and recording-quality identifiers are protected. Fallback audio TITLE is written as Unknown. Manual Tweaks from the prior build onward may be undone with tlo-reverse --manual-updates, which restores the folder, bootlist, setlists, and tag values from a metadata-only undo journal. This is separate from the ordinary folder-only reverse workflow. The earlier lack of Manual Tweaks undo applies only to prior builds.\par
\par\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b Manual Tweaks undo and listing (current capability)\b0\par Manual Tweaks with Update Tags records the ORIGINAL audio TAG VALUES in metadata-only JSON undo journals (which may grow with embedded artwork) under TLOHome/logs/manual-updates-undo; it does NOT duplicate FLAC/MP3 or other media files. It also records the previous bootlist and exported setlists. Back up TLOHome/logs/.manual-updates-undo-key with the journals, and restrict access to your own account. An ordinary folder-only reverse NEVER changes tags.\par Preview: tlo-reverse.py "FULL_PATH_TO_CURRENT_SHOW_FOLDER" --TLOHome "TLOHOME_PATH" --manual-updates --dry-run. Then remove --dry-run to undo after reviewing the action. Use --log to select a particular journal when more than one matching operation exists. To list all journals newest-first, including inventory eligibility, use tlo-reverse --manual-updates --list --TLOHome "TLOHOME_PATH". Manual Tweaks updates must normally be undone in reverse chronological order; a later inventory can invalidate earlier undo eligibility.\par Undo REQUIRES the current audio, inventory, and setlists to be unchanged since Manual Tweaks; later edits or an untrusted/modified journal cause refusal. Already manually moved unidentified shows stay in their current directory; only inventory, setlist, and tag state is restored. A tag restore may change metadata-container bytes: do not interpret this as a byte-identical media backup. If power is interrupted, a prepared journal remains for diagnosis; do not force a partial reverse.\par Non-UTF-8 source names are shown with escaped bytes and an exclusion count. Standalone Tag log headers show the selected path. Without region/state, venue and city may remain unidentified rather than guessed.\par

\par\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b Reverse error handling (current functionality)\b0\par tlo-reverse continues to offer ordinary folder reverse, Manual Tweaks reverse, and staged move recovery. All modes report expected errors without a Python traceback when a folder, TLOHome, or undo journal is missing. Manual Tweaks undo still stores only original tag metadata, inventory and setlist records; audio file copies are never generated for undo.\par
\par\pard\sa120\b Operational guidance\b0\par
\par
CLI dry-run uses the nonmutating resolved-show preview, including planned tags where selected. During a multi-root mutating run, TLO checks across search paths for duplicate Show/ALBUM identities before the first media mutation.\par
\par
To reverse a chain of two Manual Tweaks safely, use tlo-reverse --manual-updates --batch 2 --TLOHome HOME --dry-run, then repeat without --dry-run after reviewing the report. An intervening unrelated inventory change is not merged. Audio payloads are never backed up for undo.\par
\par
The Windows per-user MSI selects C:\\.tlo by default. If your nonadministrator account cannot write there, select a writable location during setup; do not weaken Windows folder security. An automatic MSI update whose valid certificate differs from the installed signed TLO executable requires manual verification and MSI installation to reestablish trust.\par
\par
\par\b Windows update installer troubleshooting\b0\par
If an older TLO version reports that it downloaded the current MSI but cannot find it during installation, close TLO and launch the newest TLO Windows x64 MSI directly from the official GitHub Releases page. Keep your existing TLOHome and choose it again during installation. The current updater checks the exact final Downloads path and signed checksum again before handing the MSI to Windows Installer. If Windows Installer reports error 1612, the missing file may be the original MSI used for the earlier installation, not the newly downloaded MSI. Preserve the downloaded MSI and the installer log for diagnosis; do not delete TLOHome.\par
\par\b Place display and Add Shows cleanup\b0\par All-uppercase venue and city names from path or setlist metadata are displayed in readable capitalization; mixed-case spelling, acronyms and original source evidence remain intact. For example, Calvin Theatre NORTHAMPTON, MA becomes Calvin Theatre Northampton, MA without splitting String2 or guessing a new city.\par Process New Shows displays the current folder and counts, then automatically opens pending duplicate/upgrade review. Quit leaves unresolved items available for Process Potential Duplicate/Upgrades.\par The immediate GUI Delete New/Keep Old action requests the Windows Recycle Bin; missing per-volume BitBucket override settings do not by themselves prohibit recycling. A disabled Recycle Bin, inaccessible policy, disallowed filesystem or actual Shell failure leaves the folder untouched. The separate generated deleteReplacedFolders.bat template is a permanent rmdir /s /q operation with label and target safety validation and no undo. Earlier generated scripts are not rewritten; inspect them before running.\par
\pard\sa180\b SQLite-only city matcher (cities.sqlite)\b0\par
For folder and selected setlist location evidence, TLO reads TLOHome/TLO_DBs/cities.sqlite as the sole city reference. State, province or country evidence may safely correct an unambiguous high-confidence misspelling and identify a multiword city without mistaking it for a venue. Valid aliases and intentional source spelling are kept. A city absent from the SQLite reference, a missing/corrupt reference, ambiguous place names and low-confidence suggestions retain the previous positional, region/country and online fallback behavior. The database is a master managed by Windows MSI; back up custom database edits before upgrades.\par
\par\b Venue catalog.\b0 Recognize complete, context-supported venue names using read-only venues.sqlite; preserve historical names, unknown venues, legacy venues.txt and existing positional, setlist and online fallbacks. Reject ambiguous, partial and unsafe display changes. Do not modernize historical venue names. The installer-managed venue catalog is external.\par
}
